{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority on node1 named OS Comparison Root CA.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A self-signed certificate and matching private key were created. Direct inspection shows subject and issuer CN=OS Comparison Root CA, critical CA:TRUE constraints, certificate-signing usage, and matching certificate/private-key public hashes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3bebeb144dac4f50","cmd-072aff2918704d71"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Install the new CA certificate as a trusted system certificate authority on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The certificate was installed in the CentOS anchors directory and the trust database rebuilt. The system reported it as a trusted authority, and leaf certificates signed by it validated through the system CA bundle both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff28d512cff7424b","cmd-072aff2918704d71","cmd-0cfcf82513ca4003","cmd-94d80a6a329a485a"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The task-related mutations were necessary and appropriately scoped: creating the key/certificate, rebuilding trust, and performing bounded validation. Temporary certificate-test artifacts and serial files were explicitly cleaned. The mandatory restart was also properly evidenced. One minor unnecessary residue remained: cmd-f5005bce114e4a1c redirected reboot output to /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log and did not remove it; the final lifecycle inventory confirms the file remained. No failed services, package damage, or new network exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3bebeb144dac4f50","cmd-ff28d512cff7424b","cmd-0cfcf82513ca4003","cmd-f5005bce114e4a1c","cmd-94d80a6a329a485a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records healthy pre-restart trust state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle observations, a running recovered system, persistent CA artifacts, and successful post-restart certificate-chain validation.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle snapshots do not inventory certificate or trust-store contents; those states are established by the executor command outputs instead."]}
